@startuml agentchannel-phase-reduction
' AgentChannel phase machine: a memoryless reduction of the bound Agent's phase.
' Source of truth: docs/src/controller/reconcilers.md (Channel phase reduction)
!include _style.puml

state "Active" as Active
state "Degraded" as Degraded
state "Failed" as Failed

[*] --> Active : first reconcile:\nagentRef resolves, Agent in\nany non-terminal phase
[*] --> Failed : first reconcile:\nagentRef does not resolve\n(AgentNotFound)

Active --> Degraded : bound Agent enters\nFailed or Degraded
Degraded --> Active : bound Agent recovers to\nany other non-terminal phase
Active --> Failed : bound Agent deleted\n(agentRef stops resolving)
Degraded --> Failed : bound Agent deleted
Failed --> Active : Agent (re)created:\nreduction resumes from\nits current phase

note right of Active
  covers Running, Idle, Hibernated,
  Resuming, Pending, Provisioning,
  and Hibernating: transient gaps are
  the delivery layer's job (wake on
  demand, bounded retry) and surface
  via PlatformConnected, not phase
end note

state "any phase" as AnyPhase #F5F5F5
state "Terminating" as Terminating

AnyPhase --> Terminating : deletion requested\n(gateway delete handshake,\nthen the finalizer)

note bottom of AnyPhase
  The machine is memoryless: phase
  is recomputed from the bound
  Agent on every reconcile, and is
  unset before the first one. It is
  one of three orthogonal axes:
  Ready reports spec validation,
  PlatformConnected reports
  delivery health.
end note

Failed -[hidden]-> AnyPhase
@enduml
